INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Kaspersky Securelist: Not just an infostealer: Gopuram backdoor deployed through 3CX supply chain attack", "source_url": "https://securelist.com/gopuram-backdoor-deployed-through-3cx-supply-chain-attack/109344/", "text": "SRC-004 findings: Kaspersky reports the 3CX infection was spread via trojanized MSI installers; a malicious DLL decrypted shellcode from the d3dcompiler_47.dll overlay, extracted C2 URLs from icons in a GitHub repository, downloaded an infostealer, and sent system information/browser history. Kaspersky observed guard64.dll in infected 3CXDesktopApp.exe; it identified this as the Gopuram backdoor, a modular backdoor capable of C2 communication, filesystem interaction, process creation, and in-memory modules. Gopuram infections increased in March 2023 and were specifically observed on cryptocurrency-company targets; fewer than ten machines in Kaspersky telemetry received Gopuram, suggesting selective deployment. Kaspersky's attribution: medium to high confidence that the 3CX campaign was attributable to Lazarus, based on Gopuram coexisting with AppleJeus on a Southeast Asian cryptocurrency-company machine in 2020; Gopuram's cryptocurrency targeting; shared loader-shellcode patterns and a C2 server (wirexpro.com) associated with AppleJeus; and oilycargo.com previously attributed to Lazarus. Kaspersky concludes Lazarus is likely the actor deploying Gopuram, and calls Gopuram the likely main/final payload. This is an independent attribution assessment and should be distinguished from Mandiant's UNC4736 cluster designation."}
