INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "WIRED: The Huge 3CX Breach Was Actually 2 Linked Supply Chain Attacks", "source_url": "https://www.wired.com/story/3cx-supply-chain-attack-times-two", "text": "SRC-008 findings: WIRED reports Mandiant identified patient zero as a 3CX employee PC compromised through an earlier Trading Technologies software supply-chain attack. The infected X_TRADER application allowed attackers to spread through 3CX, reach a software-development server, corrupt a 3CX installer, and infect many customers. WIRED says the actor was publicly described under names Kimsuky, Emerald Sleet, or Velvet Chollima and as widely believed to work for North Korea, but Mandiant's own cluster label in SRC-003 is UNC4736. Mandiant had not investigated Trading Technologies' original compromise and did not know how the application was altered or how many other victims existed. WIRED reports the X_TRADER compromise likely predated November 2021 based on a digital signature, while the 3CX follow-on attack occurred in early 2023. Kaspersky found a small number of cryptocurrency-related victims and reported selective second-stage deployment."}
